    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 231748 CCA\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n1048 AM PDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Isolated shower chances and breezy conditions stick around for a \n  few more days as a trough lingers in the region.\n\n* Drier and calmer conditions resume next week with seasonable\n  temperatures.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Thursday.\n\nThe shortwave that spurred all of the showers and storms today has \nlifted northeast, allowing drier conditions to settle in. A \nsecondary shortwave is diving south on the backside of the parent \ntrough, keeping the trough overhead today and transforming it into a \nclosed low. Cold air aloft, residual moisture, and some daytime \nsolar heating should allow some isolated instability showers (10-30% \nchances) to develop today, mainly across the northern half of the \nCWA. Most of the region stays dry though, with below normal \ntemperatures and just some breezy winds in our northwestern zones. \nThe low slowly drift east tomorrow, leaving 10-30% PoPs across \neastern Mohave County. Farther west, dry conditions are expected \nwith gusty north winds of 20-35 mph. \n\nDry conditions anticipated areawide Sunday - Thursday as the low \nfinally exits and a quasi-zonal pattern sets up. Some breezy \nconditions are possible in the southern Great Basin early in the \nweek as a shortwave moves through the PacNW, but otherwise winds \nremain light. Temperatures rebound to seasonable values and hold \nfairly steady throughout the week.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 18Z Forecast Package...\nLight winds favoring a NE direction and under 8kt persist through \nthe daytime hours, the become light out of the NW after 03-04z. \nExpect stronger north-northwesterly winds to arrive around and after \n10z with sustained speeds 10-15 kt and gusts around 25 -30 kt at \ntimes. Stronger NW winds continue into Saturday, diminishing during \nthe late afternoon and evening. Mostly clear skies last through the \nTAF period. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 18Z Forecast Package...Light and variable winds \nfavoring northerly directions persist through the day. Expect an \nincrease in N-NW winds overnight at most locations with gusts 20-30 \nkt likely. Winds increase at KBIH after 01z tonight and after 06-09z \nfor Las Vegas Valley and CRV terminals. Increased N-NW winds last \ninto the first half of the day Saturday, then likely begin \ndiminishing late afternoon and evening. Mostly clear skies last \nthrough the TAF period. \n\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Moore\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
